 halted first attempt) and the current state. Before anyone redeploys v2.3.1, it asks for the root cause of its failure and of the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CauY8Sg9fiRR8ywc1Kt6Q2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UZEUxNHZT1uDfPRpgHViqs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01V9QcZGTLtMn6SSpEBWDtGP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01C5mSNsJyNRGMLyqP4gcJSH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback only finished in us-east. Rolling back to the same version again is safe because us-east is already on v2.3.0, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XCNsNAFo71M2FtXanVCrRG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01P1Ydo2Ykf8auFpffh2feX1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JGdJ7Zwo7K3iqCW6YKsUYZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RbRh9TgVTEzdxmX6UMzcvV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished successfully. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error during rollback before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0169j8Z9tbWwgXxPEcFjwtss", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident (INC-0001) is open, so on-call has been paged.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 and its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, both failed health checks. My first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. I ran the rollback again and it finished in all three regions. The error rate is now about 0.2%, down from 18%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. It had been created, so I didn't submit a second one and page on-call twice. The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the halted first attempt) and the current state. Before anyone redeploys v2.3.1, it asks for the root cause of its failure and of the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}